// =============================================================================
// Detection: Kerberoasting - RC4 service tickets for user-account SPNs
// Lab:       Contoso Health Identity Platform  (lab/ - ITDR pack, hybrid)
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// DETECTOR ROLE (ADR 0023)
//   Microsoft Defender for Identity is the PRIMARY detector for Kerberoasting:
//   purpose-built and maintained by Microsoft (enable_defender_for_identity).
//   This rule is its portable, offline-testable twin - the same logic over DC01
//   SecurityEvent, with an SPL twin and Kusto-emulator tests - and the
//   post-trial fallback when the MDI licence lapses.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT IT CATCHES
//   A Kerberos service ticket (4769) issued with RC4-HMAC (encryption type
//   0x17) for a service that is a USER account with an SPN (not a computer
//   account, not krbtgt). An RC4 ticket is encrypted with the NT hash of the
//   service account's password, so whoever requested it can crack that
//   password offline - Kerberoasting. Rubeus / Impacket GetUserSPNs ask for
//   RC4 on purpose. In this lab svc-sql01 / svc-iis-app / svc-legacy-da are
//   the SPN accounts (lab/pam discovery flags svc-legacy-da as "Kerberoastable
//   Tier 0"); after onboarding Vault rotates them to long random passwords,
//   which is the mitigation this detection backs up.
//
// SEVERITY (dynamic - the Severity column)
//   High   : one requester asked for RC4 tickets for 3+ different services in
//            the window (a roast sweep), or for an SPN account that is in a
//            Tier-0 group (Tier0SpnAccounts).
//   Medium : a single RC4 ticket for a user SPN (an old client can still ask
//            for RC4 - check the requester before escalating).
//
// TABLE / SOURCE
//   SecurityEvent 4769 from DC01 (already in dc_event_ids, telemetry.tf).
//   Columns ServiceName, Status, TargetUserName (requester, user@REALM),
//   IpAddress. TicketEncryptionType is NOT a SecurityEvent column (Microsoft
//   Learn table reference), so it is read from the EventData XML. verify:
//   EventData's <Data Name="TicketEncryptionType"> on the first DC01 4769
//   (and that Status / ServiceName are populated for 4769). verify:
//   SecurityEvent via AMA needs Microsoft Sentinel + the "Windows Security
//   Events via AMA" connector (Microsoft Learn); without it the rows land in
//   Event - keep the rule in itdr_exclude_rules until DC01 rows are in
//   SecurityEvent. verify: "Audit Kerberos Service Ticket Operations" success
//   is on for DC01.
//
// LICENSE
//   No Entra licence. AMA ingestion billed per GB.
//
// MITRE ATT&CK
//   T1558.003 Steal or Forge Kerberos Tickets: Kerberoasting
//   Tactic: CredentialAccess
//
// FALSE-POSITIVE NOTES
//   - Legacy clients / appliances that only speak RC4 (Medium, one service).
//     Fix: set msDS-SupportedEncryptionTypes to AES on the service account.
//   - Machine accounts ($) and krbtgt are excluded: their keys are random
//     and not crackable this way.
//
// SUGGESTED SENTINEL RULE
//   Frequency 5m · Lookback 1h · one alert per row · Severity column ·
//   Entities: Account = Account / AccountDomain (the REQUESTER), IP = SourceIp,
//   Host = Host.
//
// AUTOMATED RESPONSE
//   Notify on every incident. The requester is an AD account: containment
//   takes the AD path (Invoke-AdContainment.ps1 by a human). Also rotate the
//   roasted service accounts now (lab/pam rotate.sh) - the hash may already
//   be cracking.
// =============================================================================

let LookBack = 1h;
let DcHosts = dynamic(["DC01"]);
let SweepThreshold = 3;     // distinct services per requester per window
// SPN accounts that are also Tier 0 (pam-policy.json): one RC4 ticket = High.
let Tier0SpnAccounts = dynamic(["svc-legacy-da"]);
SecurityEvent
| where TimeGenerated > ago(LookBack)
| where EventID == 4769
| extend Host = toupper(tostring(split(Computer, ".")[0]))
| where Host in (DcHosts)
| extend TicketEncryptionType = extract(@'Name="TicketEncryptionType">([^<]+)<', 1, EventData)
| where TicketEncryptionType =~ "0x17"          // RC4-HMAC
| where Status =~ "0x0"                         // ticket actually issued
| extend Service = tolower(ServiceName)
| where not(Service endswith "$") and not(Service startswith "krbtgt")
| extend Requester      = tolower(extract(@"^([^@]+)", 1, TargetUserName))
| extend RequesterRealm = extract(@"@(.+)$", 1, TargetUserName)
| where not(Requester endswith "$")
| extend SourceIp = trim_start(@"::ffff:", IpAddress)
| summarize TimeGenerated = max(TimeGenerated),
            FirstSeen     = min(TimeGenerated),
            Services      = make_set(Service, 50),
            ServiceCount  = dcount(Service),
            Tickets       = count(),
            SourceIps     = make_set(SourceIp, 10)
            by Requester, RequesterRealm, Host
| extend Tier0Roasted = array_length(set_intersect(Services, Tier0SpnAccounts)) > 0
| extend Account = Requester, AccountDomain = RequesterRealm
| extend SourceIp = tostring(SourceIps[0])
| extend Severity = iff(ServiceCount >= SweepThreshold or Tier0Roasted, "High", "Medium")
| project TimeGenerated, Severity, Account, AccountDomain, Host, SourceIp, SourceIps,
          ServiceCount, Services, Tier0Roasted, Tickets, FirstSeen
| sort by TimeGenerated desc
